In .NET 10, Android's `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` is fully deprecated (Google removed it in API 30+). MAUI now uses edge-to-edge rendering with the **WindowInsets** API instead.

**Recommended fix — use `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`** (built into MAUI):

```xml
<!-- In your page or layout wrapping the chat content -->
<ScrollView>
    <VerticalStackLayout>
        <!-- chat messages -->
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ScrollView>

<!-- Input bar at bottom -->
<Entry Placeholder="Type a message..."
       KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect="False" />
```

MAUI's `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` is **enabled by default** and automatically scrolls focused inputs into view. If it's not working for you, the most common causes are:

### 1. You explicitly disabled it
Check for this in `MauiProgram.cs` and remove it:
```csharp
// ❌ Remove this if present
Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect = true;
```

### 2. Your layout isn't inset-aware
With edge-to-edge, you need to respect safe areas. Wrap your page content so it responds to padding from system bars:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto"
      Padding="{OnPlatform Android='0,0,0,0'}"
      android:View.FitsSystemWindows="true">

    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />

    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1">
        <Entry Placeholder="Message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

### 3. Manual approach via platform code
If you need full control, handle insets in your `MainActivity`:

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
        v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

**TL;DR:** Remove any `SoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` calls, ensure `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` isn't disconnected, and let MAUI's default inset handling do the work. If your layout still doesn't respond, use the `WindowInsetsCompat` listener above.
